{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "SOLAR-CAT: Defect-engineered photocatalysts for solar hydrogen — Research Grant Proposal",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Principal Investigator: Q. Principal · Co-Investigators: R. Coinvest, S. Partner",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Summary",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Green hydrogen from direct solar water splitting could decarbonise heavy industry, but photocatalysts remain limited to < 1 % solar-to-hydrogen (STH) efficiency. SOLAR-CAT will combine in-situ spectroscopy, machine-learned defect models and high-throughput synthesis to reach 3 % STH in a 1 m² panel within 36 months.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Objectives",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "O1 — Map the link between oxygen-vacancy density and carrier lifetime in doped SrTiO₃.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "O2 — Train a surrogate model predicting STH from synthesis parameters (target MAE < 0.2 %).",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "O3 — Demonstrate a 1 m² panel with ≥ 3 % STH over 1000 h outdoor operation.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "State of the art and ambition",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The efficiency is the product of absorption, separation and surface-reaction yields:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\eta_{\\text{STH}} = \\frac{r_{\\text{H}_2}\\times\\Delta G^\\circ}{P_{\\text{sun}}\\times A} = \\eta_{\\text{abs}}\\,\\eta_{\\text{sep}}\\,\\eta_{\\text{cat}},",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:sth",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "with ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\Delta G^\\circ = 237\\ \\text{kJ mol}^{-1}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Al-doped SrTiO₃ reaches near-unity quantum efficiency in the UV ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "takata2020"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": "; SOLAR-CAT extends this to visible light.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
